<title>USA: Kansas City, Mo., okays bonds to buy light system.</title>
<headline>Kansas City, Mo., okays bonds to buy light system.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters in Kansas City, Mo., on Tuesday approved the issuance of up to $110 million of general obligation bonds, according to unofficial results from the city's election board.</p>
<p>The 18,153 to 5,818 vote gives the city the green light to issue bonds to purchase Kansas City Power and Light Co.'s share of the city lighting system, as well as upgrade and expand the system.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
